A timer line armed for a deadline nearer than any other leaves the timer where it was.
The timer would interrupt after the deadline and the thread sleep past it;
the nearest deadline the timer wakes for comes no later than any armed timer line's.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test smp-test qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line comes due before the timer wakes for it

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -42,7 +42,6 @@ void irq_set_bits(struct irq *irq, uint32_t bits)
      * and each of the others, which need not, does so once it traps.
      */
     if (line_is_timer(irq->line) && bits != 0 && tick_before(irq->deadline, nearest_deadline)) {
-        nearest_deadline = irq->deadline;
         for (uint32_t c = 0; c < CORES; c++) {
             LOOP_BOUND(CORES);
             cores[c].wake_stale = true;
